Skip the per-candidate time limit check in SuggestMgr::checkword

Upstream afde4d6 ("ofz#488133878 Timeout", in v1.7.3) makes
SuggestMgr::checkword reject every candidate once 100 ms of wall-clock
time have passed since SuggestMgr::suggest() started. In debug builds
this drops suggestions such as "crochet" for "rocet" in
MultilingualSpellCheckTest. Under HUNSPELL_CHROME_CLIENT skip this
check. The overall limit between the suggestion steps and the per-step
limits stay.

As before v1.7.3, no time check then stops twowords or ngsuggest while
they run; only the checks after each step and after ngsuggest do. So
hunspell_suggest_fuzzer can again hit the OSS-Fuzz timeout that
afde4d6 fixed.

diff --git a/src/hunspell/suggestmgr.cxx b/src/hunspell/suggestmgr.cxx
index 64797e8..c3ffa89 100644
--- a/src/hunspell/suggestmgr.cxx
+++ b/src/hunspell/suggestmgr.cxx
@@ -1858,9 +1858,11 @@ int SuggestMgr::checkword(const std::string& word,
                           int cpdsuggest,
                           int* timer,
                           std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point* timelimit) {
+#ifndef HUNSPELL_CHROME_CLIENT
   // check overall suggestion time limit
   if (std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - suggest_start > TIMELIMIT_SUGGESTION_MS)
     return 0;
+#endif
 
   // check time limit
   if (timer) {
